hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1716","Sulayman ibn Dawud meaning Abu Dawud at-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad, freedman of Abu Bakr, who said: I presented dates before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they began to join them together, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not join together."
"1717","Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, Abu Amir narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad, freedman of Abu Bakr, who used to serve the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was pleased with his service, and he said: O Abu Bakr, free Sad. He said: O Messenger of Allah, we have no servant besides him. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Free Sad; men have come to you. Abu Dawud said, meaning captives."
